from pathlib import Path
from runpy import run_path
g=run_path(str(Path(__file__).with_name('author-tools-generator.py')))
L=g['lesson']; C=g['course']

gh=[
('A workflow file','A workflow describes jobs GitHub Actions can run for a repository. The YAML file lives under .github/workflows.','name: Say hello\non: workflow_dispatch\njobs:\n  hello:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - run: echo "Hello, club"','This workflow has a manual trigger, one job and one shell step. Reading the file does not run it.','Name the file hello.yml and point to its trigger.','Running hosted workflows uses the service\'s permissions and usage rules; no run is needed to read this course.','Where does the workflow file belong?','.github/workflows','Inside a password vault'),
('Events start workflows','An event tells GitHub when to consider running a workflow. workflow_dispatch is manual; push reacts to selected pushed changes.','on:\n  push:\n    branches: [main]\n  workflow_dispatch:','The fragment allows pushes to main and manual starts. It belongs inside a complete workflow file.','Compare a branch named main with one named draft.','A filter must match the real branch name to react to its pushes.','Which branch is selected here?','main','Every branch'),
('Jobs and steps','A job runs a list of steps on a runner. Steps in one job run in order and share that job\'s working environment.','jobs:\n  explain:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - name: First step\n        run: echo "Read"\n      - name: Second step\n        run: echo "Check"','The job prints Read before Check. Separate jobs do not automatically share the same filesystem.','Add a third step named Finish.','Do not assume a file from one job appears in another job automatically.','What runs in order inside one job?','Its steps','Every job in the repository'),
('Runners execute jobs','A runner is the machine environment that executes a job. runs-on chooses a matching runner label.','runs-on: ubuntu-latest','The job asks for GitHub\'s current Ubuntu runner image. That image changes over time.','Explain why a project may need to choose an explicit supported image.','latest is a moving label, not a permanent operating-system version.','What does runs-on choose?','A runner environment','A Git branch'),
('Name steps clearly','Step names appear in the run log. Clear names help someone find the part that failed.','steps:\n  - name: Show working directory\n    run: pwd\n  - name: Print learning message\n    run: echo "Read the result"','The log groups each command under a useful name.','Write a name for a step that checks formatting.','A step name should describe its action, not claim it passed.','Why name steps?','To make run logs understandable','To store secret values'),
('Environment values','env gives a job or step named environment values. A shell can read them without repeating the literal text in each command.','env:\n  CLUB_NAME: Reading club\nsteps:\n  - run: echo "$CLUB_NAME"','In a Linux shell step, the variable expands to Reading club. This fragment belongs inside a job.','Change the message to another fictional club name.','Ordinary environment values in source are not a safe place for credentials.','What does CLUB_NAME hold?','An ordinary message value','A secure account automatically'),
('Job dependencies','needs makes a job wait for another job to succeed. This states the order between jobs.','jobs:\n  check:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - run: echo "Check"\n  report:\n    needs: check\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    steps:\n      - run: echo "Checks finished"','The report job depends on check. By default it does not run successfully past a failed needed job.','Draw the dependency arrow.','A dependency does not copy files between jobs.','What does needs: check do?','Wait for the check job','Rename the current job'),
('Matrices repeat a job','A matrix runs variations of a job. Each combination gets its own job run.','strategy:\n  matrix:\n    fruit: [apple, pear]\nsteps:\n  - run: echo "${{ matrix.fruit }}"','The fragment creates one variation for apple and one for pear. Use it within a job with a runner.','Add mango and count the variations.','A large matrix multiplies work and usage; choose useful cases.','How many variations are listed?','2','1'),
('Limit token permissions','The workflow token can be given small permissions. Give only the access a job actually needs.','permissions:\n  contents: read','The token gets read access to repository contents in this simple example. It does not need write access for a read-only check.','Explain why a test job may not need release-writing permission.','Do not give broad write permissions to untrusted changes.','Which contents permission is requested?','read','write'),
('Handle untrusted text as data','A workflow may receive text from a pull request. Do not paste untrusted text directly into a shell script; pass it as data and quote it.','env:\n  NOTE: A fixed practice message\nsteps:\n  - run: printf "%s\\n" "$NOTE"','The shell prints the value as an argument. This fixed example teaches quoting without using attacker-controlled input.','Explain why quote marks around $NOTE matter.','Never execute a message or title as if it were a trusted command.','How should untrusted text be treated?','As data','As a shell program'),
('Avoid duplicate obsolete runs','Concurrency can group related runs. cancel-in-progress can stop an older run when a newer run in the same group starts.','concurrency:\n  group: learning-${{ github.ref }}\n  cancel-in-progress: true','Runs for the same ref share the group. This can save work for checks whose old result is no longer needed.','Explain a job where cancelling halfway would need care.','Do not blindly cancel a deployment or other action that has important partial effects.','What can cancel-in-progress stop?','An older run in the same group','Every repository on GitHub'),
('Read the run result','A run log shows which jobs and steps completed. A green result means the configured commands passed, not that every product requirement was checked.','Check run:\n  syntax check: passed\n  unit tests: passed\n  visual review: not part of this workflow','The result has a clear scope. Add useful checks intentionally rather than trusting a badge alone.','Write a short report stating what this run did not check.','Never print real secrets just to diagnose a workflow.','What does a passing workflow prove?','Its configured checks passed','The whole app can never fail'),
]
C('github-actions','GitHub Actions runs automated jobs for GitHub projects. We will read small workflow files and learn events, jobs, runners and safe permissions without publishing or deploying anything.','Examples are YAML fragments or complete files as stated. Reading needs no account. Running them is a separate action in a permitted GitHub repository and may use hosted minutes.','https://docs.github.com/en/actions',[L(*r,language='yaml' if i<11 else 'text') for i,r in enumerate(gh)])

jenkins=[
('Meet a pipeline','A pipeline is a saved sequence of build or check steps. Jenkins can run it and keep a record of the result.','pipeline {\n  agent any\n  stages {\n    stage("Hello") {\n      steps { echo "Hello, club" }\n    }\n  }\n}','This declarative Jenkinsfile contains one stage that prints a message. It does not deploy anything.','Find the stage name and the step.','Jenkins is a separate automation tool; this learning app does not need a Jenkins server.','What is a pipeline?','A saved sequence of steps','A browser password'),
('Controllers and agents','The Jenkins controller coordinates work. An agent is an environment where jobs can execute.','Controller: schedules and records jobs\nAgent: runs the assigned build steps','Separating these roles helps explain where work happens. A small learning installation may look simpler, but the roles still matter.','Draw a controller assigning work to two agents.','Do not give a build more access to the host machine than it needs.','Where do assigned build steps execute?','On an agent','Inside a README file'),
('Stages show the journey','A stage groups related steps under a clear name. This helps people see where a run failed.','pipeline {\n  agent any\n  stages {\n    stage("Read") { steps { echo "Read source" } }\n    stage("Check") { steps { echo "Check source" } }\n  }\n}','The Read stage comes before Check in this sequential pipeline.','Add a Report stage.','Do not label a stage Test if it only prints a message; the example messages are demonstrations.','Why name stages?','To explain groups of work','To guarantee they pass'),
('Shell steps need the right agent','sh runs a shell command on a suitable Unix-like agent. Windows agents normally use a different step such as bat or powershell.','steps {\n  sh \'printf "Hello from the agent\\n"\'\n}','This steps fragment prints a message on a compatible agent. It belongs inside a stage.','Identify the agent operating system before choosing a shell step.','Do not assume sh exists on every agent.','What does sh require here?','A compatible shell environment','An online learner account'),
('Environment settings','An environment block provides named values to the pipeline. Use it for ordinary configuration, not hard-coded secrets.','environment {\n  CLUB_NAME = "Reading club"\n}','The setting gives later steps a shared value. This is a declarative pipeline fragment.','Choose a non-secret test mode setting.','A value written in a Jenkinsfile is visible to people who can read that file.','What belongs in this ordinary setting?','A non-secret club name','A real password'),
('Parameters let a person choose','A parameter is an input supplied when a job is started. Treat input as data and validate it before using it.','parameters {\n  booleanParam(name: "RUN_CHECKS", defaultValue: true, description: "Run the practice checks")\n}','The job presents a true-or-false choice. A default does not replace a permission check for sensitive actions.','Write a clear description for another safe boolean parameter.','Never run arbitrary parameter text as a shell command.','What kind of input is RUN_CHECKS?','Boolean','An unrestricted password'),
('Conditions skip unneeded stages','when controls whether a stage runs. It lets a pipeline state a clear condition rather than hiding it inside many shell commands.','stage("Optional check") {\n  when { expression { params.RUN_CHECKS } }\n  steps { echo "Run the chosen check" }\n}','The stage runs when the earlier boolean parameter is true.','Trace the stage when the parameter is false.','Skipping a check should be visible and intentional.','What controls this stage?','The RUN_CHECKS parameter','The stage color'),
('Always perform cleanup','A post block can run after the main stages. always is useful for cleanup or reporting whether the run passed or failed.','post {\n  always { echo "Practice run finished" }\n}','The message appears after the pipeline outcome. Real cleanup should target only resources created by that run.','Explain why cleanup may still be needed after a failure.','Do not use a broad delete command as a generic cleanup step.','When does always run?','After either success or failure','Only after success'),
('Bound a long-running step','A timeout stops waiting after a chosen limit. It keeps stuck work from occupying an agent indefinitely.','steps {\n  timeout(time: 2, unit: "MINUTES") {\n    echo "A bounded practice step"\n  }\n}','The wrapped work has a two-minute limit. This tiny echo finishes much sooner.','Choose a reasonable limit for a local unit-test step.','A timeout is a limit, not evidence that the work is correct.','What is the limit here?','2 minutes','2 hours'),
('Parallel work needs independence','Parallel branches can run independent checks at the same time. They should not accidentally change the same temporary files.','stage("Checks") {\n  parallel {\n    stage("Spelling") { steps { echo "Spelling check" } }\n    stage("Links") { steps { echo "Link check" } }\n  }\n}','The branches describe two independent checks. This fragment belongs in a declarative pipeline\'s stages.','Name two tasks that cannot safely run together.','Parallel steps that share mutable files can interfere with each other.','Which tasks suit parallel branches?','Independent tasks','Tasks that require each other\'s unfinished output'),
('Credentials stay outside source','Jenkins can provide credentials through configured bindings. A job should request only what it needs and avoid printing secret values.','Jenkinsfile: names an approved credential binding\nCredential store: holds the secret\nStep: uses it for the authorised job only','The file contains a reference, not the secret itself. Binding syntax depends on the configured credential type and plugins.','Explain why a secret should not be pasted into a build log.','Masking log output is not permission to expose secrets to untrusted code.','Where should real credentials be kept?','An approved credential store','A public Jenkinsfile'),
('Read results honestly','A Jenkins result reports the configured pipeline outcome. Useful reports explain what was actually checked and what still needs review.','Stage Check: completed\nConfigured checks: formatting only\nNot checked: browser interactions','This result is narrower than saying the application is fully tested.','Write one useful failure message for a missing practice file.','Do not confuse a successful demonstration echo with a real test suite.','What does a passing pipeline cover?','The steps it actually ran','Every possible user action'),
]
C('jenkins','Jenkins automates repeatable project jobs. We will read small Jenkinsfile examples and learn stages, agents, parameters and clear results without setting up a production automation service.','These are Jenkins Pipeline examples and fragments. Use the current official setup requirements if you later create a local disposable Jenkins installation. Nothing runs on this tutorial site.','https://www.jenkins.io/doc/book/pipeline/',[L(*r,language='groovy' if i not in [1,10,11] else 'text') for i,r in enumerate(jenkins)])
